Article 3 (Methods of Selection Examination for Clerks)
(1) Selection examinations for clerks shall consist of a written examination and an interview.
(2) The written examination shall cover the following subjects:
1. Constitutional Law;
2. Criminal Law (including Military Criminal Law);
3. Criminal Procedure (including the Military Court Act);
4. Civil Law;
5. Essay writing (meaning an essay through which general education and knowledge necessary for performing the relevant duties can be assessed).
(3) The interview shall assess ability and suitability for performing the relevant duties.
(4) Deleted on January 3, 2023.
